{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>His garments shall be torn.</b> Like קרועים, to identify him, to walk in a changed practice — or its reason is like the matter of mourning, therefore his garments shall be torn and his head bare, and the reason is that he mourns over the evil of his deeds, for because of his deeds this plague came upon him." "<b>And upon the mustache.</b> Above the mustache. The mem is from the root; the witness: ולא עשה שפמו." "<b>He shall cover.</b> In his garments, from the root of עוטה אור. The reason is that he not cause harm with the breath of his mouth." "<b>And impure.</b> Sometimes Scripture says this always when he passes along a road where there is settlement, that people may be careful and not touch him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:55.890934680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}